{
  "programId": "com.digitalarsenal.flows.terrain-refresh",
  "name": "Terrain Refresh: monthly source check",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "description": "The monthly source check of the terrain refresh (owner 2026-10-21: terrain updates run on SDN nodes as modules and flows, not as Mac scripts). One timer tick (config bodies: moon,mars, or body: moon or mars) reaches data-source/terrain-source-watch plan, which probes the 61 non-inset source files through hostcap/http-request with one-byte ranged GETs (ETag, Last-Modified and total size) and asks storage/object-s3 to list each entire raw/<naif>/ mirror prefix in R2 (SigV4 with the credential on the node's storage_r2 lane, read grant only). Each listing has no delimiter and requests up to 1000 keys, including nested <product>/ovr/<file> keys; the existing leg does not follow continuation tokens. The 32 Mars inset files exist only in raw/499/ and have no public source URL, so they are never probed. diff checks inset mirror sizes against their byte-size pins: absent object is not-mirrored, different size is size-changed, exact size is current. All 93 sources appear in the $QRP reports with the same columns; inset source_url, source_etag, source_size, source_last_modified and probe_error are empty. Public sources retain the current, source-changed, source-newer, size-changed, not-mirrored and probe-failed states. A second object-s3 sign stores each report at watch/<naif>/<yyyy-mm-dd>.qrp beside the mirror, plus one FlowNotice per body. An unreadable mirror produces a report and notice but stores nothing; inset state is then unknown. Moon and Mars together require 61 probes plus two listings, totaling 63 of the 64 input frames a node accepts per invocation, so separate runs are unnecessary and the successful listing result is not also wired to diff. This flow only observes sources and writes small report objects; quarterly re-encoding is separate. Capabilities: clock, http, and the READ grant on secrets:storage_r2 - no write grant, no storage, no wallet.",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "nodeId": "plan",
      "pluginId": "com.digitalarsenal.data-source.terrain-source-watch",
      "methodId": "plan",
      "kind": "transform",
      "capabilities": [],
      "drainPolicy": "single-shot"
    },
    {
      "nodeId": "probe",
      "pluginId": "com.digitalarsenal.hostcap.http-request",
      "methodId": "request",
      "kind": "transform",
      "capabilities": [
        "http"
      ],
      "drainPolicy": "single-shot"
    },
    {
      "nodeId": "sign_list",
      "pluginId": "com.digitalarsenal.storage.object-s3",
      "methodId": "sign",
      "kind": "transform",
      "capabilities": [
        "clock",
        "secrets:storage_r2"
      ],
      "drainPolicy": "single-shot"
    },
    {
      "nodeId": "http_list",
      "pluginId": "com.digitalarsenal.hostcap.http-request",
